-- Hosts are any device which sends or recieve traffic - computer, laptops, phones, printers, servers , cloud server, any IoT devices
   Clients and Servers
   ~initiate requests, ~Servers Respond

-- IP Address - is the identity of each host
   these are 32 bits
   Bit = 1 or 0
   Represented as four Octets
   Each Octet can be 0-255

-- Repeaters regenerate signals
   allow communications across greater distances

-- Hubs r simply multi-port repeaters
   Facilitates scaling communication b/w additional hosts
   everyone receives everyone else's data

-- Bridge sit b/w hub-connected hosts
   Bridges only have two ports
   Bridges lear which hosts are on each side

-- Switches facilitate communication within a network
   they r a combn of hubs and bridges
   - mulktiple ports
   - learns which hosts r on each port
   Hosts on a network share the same IP address space

-- Routers facilitate communication b/w networks
   Provides a traffic control pouint ( security, filtering, redirecting)
   traditionally, switches could not perform such filtering
   - Gateway - each hosts way out of their local network eg ip add - 172.16.20.33, default gateway - 172.16.20.1

-- Diffrenece
  routing is the process of moving data between netwroks
  switching is the process of moving data withing networks

-- OSI MODEL
  -- Layer 1 - Physical - Transporting Bits
     Computer data exists in the form of bits ( 1's and 0's)
     something has to transport these bits b/w hosts
     L1 technologies : cables, wifi, repeaters, hubs 
  -- Layer 2 - Data Link
               

